====================================================================================================
A. the signal speed of a supported medium is the circular velocity, whatever supports it
====================================================================================================
  solid at its stall (delta = 1600): c_T = sqrt(g r / ln delta) = 405 km/s
  polytrope in the well:            c_s = sqrt(|Psi|) ~ 778 km/s
  superfluid core:                  c_s ~ v_c = 1100 km/s
  merger speed 3000 km/s (shock 4700): Mach in the medium = 7.4 (solid), 3.9 (polytrope), 2.7 (superfluid)
  [PASS] A1 every supported medium is supersonic in a Bullet-class merger: v_merge / c >= 2.5 for the solid, the polytrope and the superfluid core

====================================================================================================
B. the lag: a supported medium re-pins on L/c, and trails the galaxies by v_merge L / c
====================================================================================================
  solid      : response time L/c = 0.48 Gyr, lag = 1482 kpc   (observed peak-galaxy offset <= 50 kpc)
  polytrope  : response time L/c = 0.25 Gyr, lag = 771 kpc   (observed peak-galaxy offset <= 50 kpc)
  superfluid : response time L/c = 0.18 Gyr, lag = 545 kpc   (observed peak-galaxy offset <= 50 kpc)
  to keep the lag under 50 kpc the medium needs c >= v_merge L/dx = 12000 km/s = 0.040 c -- a hot medium, which the forest and the CMB forbid (pincer C4, G3)
  [PASS] B1 the lag of every supported medium exceeds the observed peak-galaxy offset by > 10x (Bullet cluster)   (min lag / max offset = 11)

====================================================================================================
C. no pass-through: elastic capacity vs collision energy
====================================================================================================
  solid: E_kin / E_elastic,max ~ v_merge^2 / (2 c_T^2) = 27: the collision cannot be stored and returned elastically; a supersonic (Mach 7) impact of two single-valued media shocks and merges into ONE central peak
  observed: TWO dark peaks, each on the far side of its gas, receding (Clowe+ 2006; Markevitch+ 2004) -- the cores passed through each other
  [PASS] C1 the solid's elastic capacity falls short of the Bullet's collision energy by > 10x: no rebound, and no pass-through for any single-valued medium   (ratio = 27)

====================================================================================================
D. what the peaks need: MOND phantom of the stars vs the lensing mass at the galaxies' position
====================================================================================================
  canonical : g_N(stars, 250 kpc) = 2.23e-11 m/s^2 = 0.24 a_0 -> nu = 2.28, MOND dynamical mass = 2.3e+13 Msun vs lensing 2.3e+14: short by 10x; ballistic dark mass required ~ 2.1e+14 Msun
  alt       : g_N(stars, 250 kpc) = 2.23e-11 m/s^2 = 0.20 a_0 -> nu = 2.46, MOND dynamical mass = 2.5e+13 Msun vs lensing 2.3e+14: short by 9x; ballistic dark mass required ~ 2.1e+14 Msun
  [PASS] D1 MOND + the subcluster's stars fall short of the lensing peak by > 5x on both footings: the peak is ~2e14 Msun of something that moved ballistically with the galaxies   (min shortfall = 9x)

====================================================================================================
E. the class verdict, and the counter-datum
====================================================================================================
  supported media (polytrope, solid, superfluid core, any pinned condensate) : c ~ v_c  ->  lag ~ Mpc, no pass-through  ->  EXCLUDED by the Bullet
  ballistic particles (CDM, WDM, sterile neutrinos)                          : pass through, no lag                       ->  allowed by the Bullet
  linearly superposable waves (fuzzy DM)                                      : solitons pass through with interference       ->  allowed; but the forest needs m >= 2e-20 eV,
                                                                                whose de Broglie length is sub-kpc: it forms galaxy halos like CDM (the pincer's double count returns)
  El Gordo (z = 0.87, v ~ 2500 km/s, Menanteau+ 2012): the same lag argument, x0.8 the Bullet's.  Abell 520: a dark core at the gas position (Jee+ 2012),
  disputed (Clowe+ 2012); if real it would favour a lagging medium in that one system.  Recorded; it does not remove the Bullet.

====================================================================================================
VERDICT
====================================================================================================
  Cluster mergers are a signal-speed meter for the dark component, and the reading is unambiguous: whatever carries the ~2e14 Msun
  under the Bullet's galaxies moved with them at 3000 km/s and passed through its twin.  No medium that holds itself up in a well can
  do that -- its speed is the circular velocity, 5-10x too slow -- and no single-valued medium can pass through itself.  The solid,
  the polytrope and the superfluid core all fail here, after passing everything else.  What survives is ballistic (or a superposable
  wave), and ballistic-and-cold forms galaxy halos.  The road to 'no dark matter' ends at the Bullet cluster, from a new direction.

